From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:41:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Leave a window that draws its own caption
 undecorated.

A window with a caption style whose client area reaches up into where
the caption would be draws the caption itself, keeping of the frame no
more than the desktop window manager of Windows 10 and later draws; a
window manager asked to decorate it added a second title bar over the
application's own, which the smaller visible rectangle then cut into.
Office takes this frame once DWM answers it as Windows 11 does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1af6bd6169a357ba9a2a7d3c8f88068a644f594e)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index 72856bff38d..0a7325f0d45 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -2147,6 +2147,12 @@ static RECT get_visible_rect( HWND hwnd, BOOL shaped, UINT style, UINT ex_style,
     if (!user_driver->pGetWindowStyleMasks( hwnd, style, ex_style, &style_mask, &ex_style_mask )) return rects->window;
     if (!adjust_window_rect( &rect, style & style_mask, FALSE, ex_style & ex_style_mask, round_dpi( dpi ) )) return rects->window;
 
+    /* A caption the application draws in its client area, keeping of the frame no more than the desktop window
+     * manager of Windows 10 and later draws around it, leaves a window manager nothing to decorate. */
+    if ((style & style_mask & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION && !(style & WS_MINIMIZE) &&
+        rects->client.top - rects->window.top < -rect.top)
+        return rects->window;
+
     visible_rect = rects->window;
     visible_rect.left   -= rect.left;
     visible_rect.right  -= rect.right;
